BanMido wrote:
>
> I read on the wiki that all major demons are immune to death rays, so
> no need to give the shield of reflection I found on Medusa's island to
> my balrog, right?

Try any sort of armor you think your pet will wear.  More is better.  Go
for the shield.

> What about weapons and other stuff, anything useful
> I should give to my pet balrog?

Do you know of the list of non-artifact weapons preferences by monsters?
If you know that list try the best spare weapon you have near the front
of the list.  I often have a spare long sword and always have an
assortment of spare elven broadswords.  There's a story line argument
for giving a pet balrog a weapon in the broadsword class.

If I understand the artifact code correctly pets will pick up any
non-cursed artifact that is of their alignment or unaligned.  Balrogs
are lawful.  According to the code they will wield the first artifact in
their inventory so it should look random whether they switch to the new
artifact or not.  It might be amuzing to hand it Demonbane and see what
happens.


